1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
You live abroad, and you're building
a house back home.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,500
Every month you send money,
and you get photos on your phone.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:12,000
Were they taken on your plot?
This week?

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Plotwatch replaces trust with evidence.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Brice lives in Canada. He's funding
a five-storey residence in Yaoundé.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Plotwatch shows him the build stage by stage,
and what needs him now.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Every photo is taken with the app's camera,
on the plot.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The server checks it: inside the site boundary,
accurate GPS, its own clock,

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
and the photo's fingerprint. Verified.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
When a check fails, Plotwatch says so.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
This one is only partly verified:
the GPS fix was weak.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
When the site manager submits a stage,
Brice is notified at once.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
He approves it,
or sends it back with a comment.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
On site, Joseph uses the Android app:
the checklist, the camera,

15
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
updates from the site,
and payments to confirm.

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Every payment and expense goes into
a shared ledger, with receipt photos.

17
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Entries are never edited, only reversed.

18
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:45,000
And Plotwatch flags thirty-three million francs
not yet backed by a receipt.

19
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,500
Plotwatch is built with Flutter and Serverpod:
live streams, scheduled tasks,

20
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:55,000
verified uploads and authentication,
on Serverpod Cloud.

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Try it at plotwatch.serverpod.space.
